and that you want to know whether he can bring him in to eat. So the women walked inside and they asked the waitress if Curtis could come inside to join them. And the lady said, of course, no problem at all. So as long as I was that boy and their driver, I could eat with them at a table in a restaurant, but if I were equal to them, I could not. This kind of humiliation on the road was routine and had been going on for decades.
想问问能不能让他进来一起吃饭。于是女士们走进餐馆，问服务员柯蒂斯是否可以进来加入她们。那位女士说，当然，没问题。所以，只要我是那个“男孩”和她们的司机，我就能和她们坐在餐馆里吃饭；但如果我和她们平等，我就不能。这种在路上的羞辱是家常便饭，而且已经持续了几十年。

