and started working on the guide full time. He even opened an affiliated travel agency that helped tourists arrange trips. But still, there was the challenge full time. He even opened an affiliated travel agency that helped tourist arrange trips. But still there was the challenge of distribution. How to get the guide into the hands of travelers who needed it. That happened in a few ways. The United States travel bureau signed on to help out and then there were the more informal networks. Well churches, Pullman Portters, the Urban League, the NWCP, the Masonic lodges. There was a very wide, very distribution process in place for these green books. And there was an important corporate. There's a smile for every mile at the SO sign.
开始全职从事指南的工作。他甚至开设了一家附属旅行社，帮助游客安排行程。但仍然存在分销的挑战。如何将指南送到需要的旅行者手中。这通过几种方式实现。美国旅游局签约提供帮助，还有一些更非正式的网络。教堂、普尔曼搬运工、城市联盟、全国有色人种协进会、共济会会所。这些《绿皮书》有一套非常广泛的分销流程。还有一个重要的企业合作伙伴。在埃索（Esso）标志下，每一英里都有一个微笑。

